{"id": "EUVD-2026-104285", "enisaUuid": "58173343-a30c-35db-b87c-d598efbf949a", "description": "Krayin CRM 2.2.5 before 2.2.7 contains a server-side request forgery filter bypass that allows users with webhook permissions to reach internal addresses via DNS rebinding. Attackers can return a public address during WebhookService::isSafeEndpoint() validation and an internal address when Guzzle re-resolves, sending blind requests to internal services and cloud metadata endpoints.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:54:40", "baseScore": 2.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/pull/2683", "https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/commit/64b9125f33a7eb2ef9916d0e5fd8215c7f6a8c28", "https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/blob/v2.2.6/packages/Webkul/Automation/src/Services/WebhookService.php", "https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/releases/tag/v2.2.7", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/krayin-crm-2.2.5-before-2.2.7-ssrf-filter-bypass-via-dns-rebinding"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xjh5-97m9-9vqf", "CVE-2026-112288"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "93ca4f5d-4318-318b-bf34-a10e11dcad40", "product": {"name": "laravel-crm", "vendor": {"name": "krayin"}}, "product_version": "2.2.5 <2.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1c1e310e-79e9-3640-b834-8b7b7449dd7e", "vendor": {"name": "krayin"}}], "isExploited": false}